# -*- ThePEG-repository -*-
##############################################################################
# THE SAME POWHEG-V2 LHE EVENTS, SHOWERED AND HADRONISED BY HERWIG 7.
#
# nu_mu p -> mu- X at Q2 > 4 GeV2, the neutrino charged-current benchmark --
# the counterpart of LHE-mu.in, which CONVENTIONS.md rule 2b requires and which
# carries the same argument.  The matrix element, the matching, the parton
# distribution and the scale all come from the Les Houches file -- the SAME
# file powheg/run_powheg_v2.sh hands to Pythia 8 for the published `powheg_nu`
# sample -- so the only difference between the two samples is the shower and
# the hadronisation model:
#
#     Pythia 8.311   p_T-ordered dipole shower + Lund string
#     Herwig 7.3.0   angular-ordered shower + cluster model
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (user, 2026-09-08).  The hadronisation model was confounded
# with the generator everywhere in this benchmark: every Lund-string number
# came from Pythia or from something showered by Pythia, every cluster number
# from Sherpa's AHADIC or Herwig's own matrix element.  One matrix element
# through two independent showers is the only comparison here in which the
# hadronisation model is the thing that changes.
#
# AND IT IS ALSO THE SHOWER STUDY AT NLO.  `pythia8/shower/` switches
# PartonShowers:model on the LO samples, because on a POWHEG sample Pythia's
# veto hooks are a SimpleShower feature and Vincia and Dire deliver nothing
# (0 and 225 events of 59775; logs/shower_probe_powheg.log).  Herwig applies
# the POWHEG veto through its own machinery -- MaxPtIsMuF/RestrictPhasespace
# below -- so this path carries an NLO-matched shower comparison that the
# PartonShowers:model switch cannot.
#
# WHAT IS HELD FIXED, deliberately and item by item: the proton PDF
# (NNPDF4.0 NNLO, for the backward evolution as well as the hard process),
# no multiple interactions, no QED radiation in the shower, the ctau > 10 mm
# stability convention, and the 0.5 GeV intrinsic pT this benchmark needs at
# sqrt(s) = 43 GeV (see DIS-mu-POWHEG.in for the measurement).  Anything
# Herwig tunes that Pythia does not is part of "the hadronisation model", and
# that is what the figure is about.
#
# @LHEFILE@ and @RUNNAME@ are substituted per job by
# powheg/run_powheg_herwig.sh; this template holds no path of its own
# (CONVENTIONS.md rule 1).
#
# ONE DIFFERENCE FROM THE MUON CARD BEYOND THE BEAM NAME, and it is worth
# knowing: POWHEG-V2 already writes this side in the lepton-proton c.m.
# frame, with both beams near 21.66 GeV, so tools/lhe_boost_cm.py passes the
# file through untouched.  The muon side is written fixed-target, with the
# proton AT REST and therefore with no momentum at all, which is what makes
# the boost necessary there and nowhere else.
#
# usage (via the driver): Herwig read <job>/LHE-nu.in ; Herwig run <run>.run
##############################################################################

# EPCollider.in is the lepton-hadron setup: EPExtractor, MPI off on every
# shower handler, the lepton-line QED splittings deleted, and
# KinematicsReconstructor:ReconstructionOption Colour.  It also configures the
# standard EventHandler, which the Les Houches handler below REPLACES -- the
# settings that matter here are the global ones.
read snippets/EPCollider.in

##################################################
# proton PDF: NNPDF4.0 NNLO, the set POWHEG ran with
##################################################
cd /Herwig/Partons
create ThePEG::LHAPDF NNPDF40 ThePEGLHAPDF.so
set NNPDF40:PDFName NNPDF40_nnlo_as_01180
set NNPDF40:RemnantHandler HadronRemnants
set /Herwig/Particles/p+:PDF NNPDF40
set EPExtractor:SecondPDF NNPDF40
set /Herwig/Shower/ShowerHandler:PDFB NNPDF40

##################################################
# the Les Houches event handler
##################################################
cd /Herwig/EventHandlers
library LesHouches.so
create ThePEG::LesHouchesEventHandler LesHouchesHandler
# EPExtractor, NOT the template's PPExtractor: beam A is a lepton and takes no
# parton distribution.  PPExtractor would ask the muon for a PDF.
set LesHouchesHandler:PartonExtractor /Herwig/Partons/EPExtractor
set LesHouchesHandler:CascadeHandler /Herwig/Shower/ShowerHandler
set LesHouchesHandler:DecayHandler /Herwig/Decays/DecayHandler
set LesHouchesHandler:HadronizationHandler /Herwig/Hadronization/ClusterHadHandler
# POWHEG-V2 writes IDWTUP = -4: weighted events that may be negative.
set LesHouchesHandler:WeightOption VarNegWeight
set /Herwig/Generators/EventGenerator:EventHandler \
    /Herwig/EventHandlers/LesHouchesHandler

# NO CUTS AT THIS STAGE.  The fiducial region is applied by the analysis, and
# a generation-level cut here would act on the SHOWERED event rather than on
# the Born one -- which is the SimpleDISCut trap of CONVENTIONS.md rule 2 in a
# different costume.  For a POWHEG sample it would also cut the extra jet,
# which the matching forbids.
create ThePEG::Cuts /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts
# EVERY LIMIT SPELLED OUT, because the defaults are not all finite.  A bare
# Cuts object carries infinite rapidity limits, and saverun then dies with
# "Tried to write a NaN or Inf double to a persistent stream" -- after having
# already written a .run file, which then fails to read back.  The values
# below are wide enough to cut nothing at these energies, and none of them
# is exactly zero: ThePEG builds the parton bins from log(x_min) and log of a
# zero limit is -inf.  x > 1e-9 cuts nothing -- the fiducial region reaches
# x ~ 2e-3 at 1 TeV.
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:MHatMin 0.1*GeV
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:MHatMax 1.0e7*GeV
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:ScaleMin 1.0e-6*GeV2
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:ScaleMax 1.0e14*GeV2
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:X1Min 1.0e-9
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:X1Max 1.0
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:X2Min 1.0e-9
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:X2Max 1.0
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:YHatMin -100.0
set /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts:YHatMax 100.0

create ThePEG::LesHouchesFileReader LesHouchesReader
set LesHouchesReader:FileName @LHEFILE@
set LesHouchesReader:AllowedToReOpen No
set LesHouchesReader:InitPDFs 0
set LesHouchesReader:Cuts /Herwig/Cuts/NoCuts
# IDWTUP = -4 IS NOT A READER MODE ThePEG KNOWS.  Left alone it prints a
# warning saying it will "make intelligent guesses to get correct
# statistics" and carries on -- the shape of failure CONVENTIONS.md rule 2 is
# about.  Weighted On says explicitly that the events carry weights, which
# is what -4 means, and the analysis normalises from the weight sum anyway.
set LesHouchesHandler:Weighted On
# rounding in the Les Houches record: rescale the energy to close momentum
set LesHouchesReader:MomentumTreatment RescaleEnergy
# BEAM A IS THE NEUTRINO AND HAS NO PARTON CONTENT.  Saying so takes two
# statements, not one: the reader's own PDFA, and the muon particle's, which
# is what the parton extractor consults when it builds the parton bins.
# Without them the run dies at initialisation with "Could not find
# appropriate PartonBin objects", which names neither the beam nor the muon.
set /Herwig/Particles/nu_mu:PDF /Herwig/Partons/NoPDF
set LesHouchesReader:PDFA /Herwig/Partons/NoPDF
set LesHouchesReader:PDFB /Herwig/Partons/NNPDF40
insert LesHouchesHandler:LesHouchesReaders 0 LesHouchesReader

##################################################
# POWHEG matching: SCALUP is a VETO scale
##################################################
cd /Herwig/Shower
# The hardest emission is already in the file.  HardEmission must stay None:
# turning it on would have Herwig generate a second hardest emission on top of
# POWHEG's, which is the double count the veto exists to prevent.
set ShowerHandler:HardEmission None
set ShowerHandler:MaxPtIsMuF Yes
set ShowerHandler:RestrictPhasespace Yes
# wide-angle radiation, as recommended for POWHEG input
set PartnerFinder:PartnerMethod Random
set PartnerFinder:ScaleChoice Partner
# the intrinsic pT this benchmark runs at -- 0.5 GeV, not Herwig's LHC-tuned
# 2.2, which discards 5.9% of muon and 2.5% of neutrino events at
# sqrt(s) = 43 GeV, biased to low Q2.  The measurement is in
# DIS-mu-POWHEG.in.
set ShowerHandler:IntrinsicPtGaussian 0.5*GeV

##################################################
# no QED radiation off the quark line (the lepton line is already done by
# EPCollider.in), matching the Pythia card's four QEDshowerBy* switches
##################################################
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting u->u,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting d->d,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting s->s,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting c->c,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting b->b,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteFinalSplitting t->t,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting u->u,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting d->d,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting s->s,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting c->c,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting b->b,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting t->t,gamma; /Herwig/Shower/QtoQGammaSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting d->gamma,d; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting u->gamma,u; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting s->gamma,s; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting c->gamma,c; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov
do SplittingGenerator:DeleteInitialSplitting b->gamma,b; /Herwig/Shower/QtoGammaQSudakov

##################################################
# stable-particle convention: ctau > 10 mm stable
##################################################
set /Herwig/Decays/DecayHandler:MaxLifeTime 10*mm

##################################################
# HepMC3 Ascii output, the format analysis/analyze.py reads
##################################################
cd /Herwig/Generators
read snippets/HepMC.in
set /Herwig/Analysis/HepMC:Format GenEventHepMC3
set /Herwig/Analysis/HepMC:Filename events.hepmc
set /Herwig/Analysis/HepMC:PrintEvent 100000000
set /Herwig/Analysis/HepMC:Units GeV_mm

set EventGenerator:MaxErrors 10000
set EventGenerator:NumberOfEvents 100000000
set EventGenerator:PrintEvent 0

# REBUILD, DO NOT REPLACE (2026-09-19, patches/thepeg-2.3.0-event-error-retry.diff):
# an event whose remnant Herwig cannot put on shell is re-showered from the SAME
# Les Houches event instead of being dropped for the next one.  The drops were
# charm/sea/high-x (v2 nu 1 TeV p: charm 19.13% in the LHE, 16.97% delivered
# without this, 19.67% with it).  Needs the patched ThePEG: unpatched, read fails.
set /Herwig/EventHandlers/LesHouchesHandler:MaxEventErrorRetries 100
# ... and never move the scattered lepton to rescue the remnant: the event
# fails and is re-showered instead (herwig7/production/make_cards.py, RETRIES).
set /Herwig/Partons/RemnantDecayer:DISRemnantOption NoLepton
saverun @RUNNAME@ EventGenerator
